  "notes": "Derivative FRO is CIBOR2 (fixing T-2). LCH/Eurex switched DKK PAI/discounting to DESTR flat on 22-Nov-2025 - DESTR OIS swap family not yet configured here, so SELF-discounting is an approximation for cleared DKK. CITA T/N swaps dead since 1-Jan-2026. Probed 2026-07: DKSO{n}/DKSWTN{n} resolve as DKK SWAP OIS / T/N INDEXED but carry NO composite/BGN prices; DESTR Index and DETNT/N Index fixings ARE live. Par DESTR OIS is dealer-run only for now. Front end 2026-08-03: direct 6M IMM FRAs DKF60101/DKF60201 (live; 0301+ resolve but no px) — exactly what Bloomberg's YCSW0339 builds from (CIBO06M + DKF60201 + DKSW2..). Replaced the 3M-strip+DKBFVC-basis frontFromOis synthesis, which sat -10 to -16bp off S0339 sub-1y (the basis model, not the strip, was the error term). If the DKF6 quotes die, the old frontFromOis block (3M strip DKF30001-0701 + DKBFVC basis) is in git history pre-6.2.6. DKSW1/DKSW1F DISABLED same day: both print live-looking composites but sit ~+17bp RICH vs the FRA-implied 6-12M path (DKSW1 2.936 vs CIBOR + DKF6 strip ~2.9-3.0 window), which kinked 6M6M +12bp — Bloomberg's own curve omits them for the same reason (its 12M point is the 2nd IMM FRA). Re-enable only if their contributors come back in line with the strip. DESTR OIS added 2026-07: DKSWD{x} family (user-supplied root; 1M-30Y live, composite-only full securities). Discounting stays SELF off CIBOR - NOTE LCH/Eurex PAI is DESTR flat since Nov-2025, so switching discounting to OIS is the correct next step for cleared DKK but is a deliberate re-marking.",
